# 🌐 Networking Fundamentals

> Building a strong networking foundation for cybersecurity and web application penetration testing.

---

## 📖 About This Repository

This repository contains my notes, practical exercises, and Linux networking commands completed while learning the fundamentals of computer networking.

The goal is to understand how devices communicate over a network before moving on to web application penetration testing.

---

## 🎯 Topics Covered

* ✅ What is a Network?
* ✅ LAN vs WAN
* ✅ IP Address (IPv4 & IPv6)
* ✅ MAC Address
* ✅ Router
* ✅ Switch
* ✅ Gateway
* ✅ DNS
* ✅ DHCP
* ✅ TCP vs UDP
* ✅ Ports
* ✅ HTTP vs HTTPS
* ✅ Cookies & Sessions
* ✅ DNS Records

  * A Record
  * AAAA Record
  * MX Record
  * CNAME Record
  * TXT Record
  * NS Record

---

## 💻 Linux Commands Practiced

```bash
ip a
ip route
hostname -I
ping google.com
arp -a
ip neigh
nslookup google.com
dig google.com
host google.com
curl https://example.com
wget https://example.com
```

